Mount Virtual Filesystems and Enter Chroot Environment

1. Copy host DNS settings so internet access works inside chroot:

`cp -v /etc/resolv.conf $KLFS/etc/`

2. Bind-mount host virtual pseudo-filesystems:

`mount -v --bind /dev $KLFS/dev`
`mount -v --bind /dev/pts $KLFS/dev/pts`
`mount -vt proc proc $KLFS/proc`
`mount -vt sysfs sysfs $KLFS/sys`
`mount -vt tmpfs tmpfs $KLFS/run`

3. Enter the chroot environment with clean environment variables:

`chroot "$KLFS" /usr/bin/env -i HOME=/root TERM="$TERM" PS1="(klfs chroot) \u:\w\$"  PATH=/bin/busybox:/bin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/usr/sbin /bin/sh`
